`RobotConfigurationEditor` owns an independent copy of a robot configuration. The constructor and `setIdentity` require `nickname` and `zone` to contain non-whitespace text, trim accepted values, and throw `TypeError` otherwise. `getConfiguration` returns a fresh copy. `rotateSecret` requires all three secret strings to be non-empty, throws `RangeError` unless `nextSecret` and `confirmation` are identical, then calls `acceptCurrent` exactly once with `currentSecret`. If that callback returns false, return false without changing the secret. If it returns true, store `nextSecret` and return true. Validation failures and callback exceptions must leave state unchanged. No method may expose an alias to stored state.

